@startuml failover
title US-07: Failover - Follower Takes Over When Leader Crashes

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam participantBorderColor #555555
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7

participant "Evaluator\nInstance A\n(leader)" as A
participant "Evaluator\nInstance B\n(follower)" as B
database "Redis\nalert-evaluator:leader" as Redis
queue "Kafka\nalerts" as Kafka

A -> Kafka : emitting alerts normally
A -> Redis : renewing lease (heartbeat)

note over A
  Instance A crashes.
  Lease renewal stops.
  TTL counts down.
end note

A ->x A : crash

loop follower polling
  B -> Redis : GET alert-evaluator:leader
  Redis --> B : $instance_a (lease still held)
end

note over Redis
  TTL expires.
  Key is automatically deleted.
end note

Redis -> Redis : key expired and deleted

B -> Redis : SET alert-evaluator:leader $instance_b NX PX $TTL_MS
Redis --> B : OK (lease acquired - Instance B is now leader)

note over B
  Failover complete within one TTL window.
  No manual intervention required.
  No duplicate alerts emitted during transition
  as B was not evaluating while A held the lease.
end note

B -> Kafka : emit alerts (new leader)

@enduml
